node_modules/
dist/

# .env is NOT excluded here (unlike a typical backend .dockerignore) — Vite
# only ever exposes vars explicitly prefixed VITE_ to client code, so by
# Vite's own design there is nothing secret to protect: a VITE_ var is
# guaranteed to end up in the shipped JS bundle regardless of whether it's
# read from this file or a --build-arg. Excluding it just breaks build-time
# config like VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID silently (the value is undefined, not an
# error) instead of protecting anything. It's also moot for image size/leak
# concerns either way: the Dockerfile's final stage only ever COPYs `dist/`
# out of the build stage, never the build stage's own filesystem, so this
# file doesn't persist into the shipped image even if it did contain
# something non-VITE_-prefixed.
